AB  - Public procurement is one of the most prominent issues due to its share in public expenditures and its impact on the welfare of society. Corruption, which causes public procurement or procurement processes to fail to function properly, is prevented in various ways, both in developed and other economies. Blockchain is a type of distributed ledger and represents a fundamental change in record-keeping. Features of blockchain technology such as its decentralized structure, permanence, traceability, and auditability, lead to an increase in studies on the applicability of this technology to public procurement processes. Although it is still a developing technology, applications show that blockchain has great potential for preventing corruption in public procurement. In this context, the study examines the potential of this technology in reducing corruption in public procurement on the basis of practice and literature and aims to contribute to the literature and create a theoretical framework for subsequent studies.
