AB  - This study examines the impact of digital government on public expenditures in Arab countries with varying levels of corruption during the period from 2003 to 2020. The study employed a panel data methodology (panel models) and concluded that the overall impact of digital government development on public expenditures is negative, and this impact increases with higher levels of corruption. The results also showed that digital government has a direct negative effect on public expenditures, in addition to an indirect effect through the level of corruption as a mediating variable.
