AB  - This article addresses the vision of Sustainable Development 2030, focusing on opportunities for governmental transformation and combating corruption. The research highlights the importance of anti-corruption strategies as a fundamental condition for achieving the seventeen Sustainable Development Goals. It indicates that digital governmental transformation enhances economic well-being and reduces social disparities. The article also discusses the impact of administrative and financial corruption on the economy and society, emphasizing the need for bold steps by countries to confront this phenomenon. Additionally, the articles cover economic and social topics in the Arab world, including the experience of Singapore and the importance of good governance in rationalizing public spending and reducing poverty.
