AB  - The 31st Volume of the journal Sosyoekonomi presents twenty-one studies on socioeconomic topics. The issue focuses on research articles and econometric models for practical applications, with limited inclusion of surveys, reviews, and theoretical studies. The studies cover a range of topics, including the impact of social support on work-family life satisfaction, the profitability of companies in the airline transportation sector, the role of institutional structure in monetary policy, and the use of drones for commercial product deliveries. Other studies explore the service quality of preschool education institutions, the significance of asset quality in Islamic microfinance institutions, and the impact of democracy and political stability on economic growth. The issue also includes studies on the informal economy and corruption, green supply, the effects of the COVID-19 pandemic on various industries, the ecological footprint, and the geography of the Turkic World as a tourist destination. The issue concludes with studies on energy production sources, the impact of blockchain and the Internet of Things on business performance, and the convergence of public expenditures among European Union member countries.
