AB  - One factor that has delayed growth in the Western Balkans is the high level of corruption. Political instability and inefficiency of governments has generated corruption, which halts GDP growth and depresses private and foreign investment. The results of the empirical analysis suggest that corruption has a positive but very weak impact on real GDP per capita growth, perhaps a low level of corruption can reduce bureaucracy and this can stimulate economic growth. We also analyze the impact of the components public spending on corruption. The results in this case suggest that public spending could have a positive impact on the growth of corruption, but the result in this case is not robust.
